# Lux — .NET solution
#
# Only this directory is published; everything else in the project (oracle dumps, captures, the Wine prefix,
# vendor binaries, Ghidra projects) lives outside it and is backed up locally instead.

# ---- build output -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
bin/
obj/
[Bb]uild/
[Oo]ut/
artifacts/
*.binlog

# NuGet
*.nupkg
*.snupkg
.nuget/
packages/
!packages/build/
project.lock.json
project.assets.json

# ---- IDE / editor -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
.vs/
.vscode/
.idea/
*.user
*.suo
*.userosscache
*.sln.docstates
*.userprefs
*.swp
*~
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# ---- test / coverage / profiling ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
[Tt]est[Rr]esult*/
coverage*.json
coverage*.xml
coverage*.info
*.coverage
*.coveragexml
*.trx
BenchmarkDotNet.Artifacts/
*.dotCover
*.psess
*.vsp
*.vspx

# ---- local scratch ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# `_spike/` is a throwaway experiment area kept out of history deliberately.
_spike/
*.received.*
*.orig
*.rej
*.bak

# ---- outputs a run may drop in the tree ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# The CLI writes exports beside the input by default; if anyone points it at the solution directory, these keep
# multi-hundred-megabyte DNGs and captures out of a commit. Source data lives outside this directory entirely.
*.lri
*.dng
*.jpg
*.jpeg
*.ppm
*.hdr
*.f32

# The three embedded lookup tables under Pipeline/**/Data are REQUIRED by the build (see the EmbeddedResource
# entries in Lux.Engine.csproj) and are deliberately re-included past the patterns above.
!Lux.Engine/Pipeline/**/*.bin

# Sample captures and outputs shipped with the repo: everything under Samples/ is versioned,
# regardless of the output-type patterns above. Keep each file well under GitHub's 100 MB limit.
!Samples/
!Samples/**
